  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0154379a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 6 — (Optional) Logistic-regression-ready frame\n",
    "\n",
    "A parallel table for linear models: it adds explicit missingness flags and one-hot encodes categoricals.\n",
    "Linear models cannot consume NaNs natively, so this branch needs in-fold median imputation + scaling\n",
    "(noted below). It is exported but not used by the tree-based ensemble."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 33,
   "id": "b8b87c5b-f98e-4e8c-b13d-9a24c27cc91c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Missingness flags created: 90\n",
      "df_logistic shape: (356251, 690)\n",
      "Remaining NaNs: 11627616\n",
      "TARGET missing: 48744\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Build the linear-model variant: one binary FLAG_MISSING_* per NaN column\n",
    "# (so the model still 'sees' missingness after imputation), then one-hot encode\n",
    "# the remaining categoricals.\n",
    "\n",
    "df_logistic = df_main.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create missingness flags for all columns with NaNs before imputing\n",
    "nan_cols = [c for c in df_logistic.columns if df_logistic[c].isnull().any() and c != \"TARGET\"]\n",
    "for col in nan_cols:\n",
    "    df_logistic[f\"FLAG_MISSING_{col}\"] = df_logistic[col].isnull().astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Missingness flags created: {len(nan_cols)}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# One-hot encode remaining categorical columns\n",
    "cat_cols = df_logistic.select_dtypes(include=[\"object\"]).columns.tolist()\n",
    "df_logistic = pd.get_dummies(df_logistic, columns=cat_cols, dummy_na=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"df_logistic shape:\", df_logistic.shape)\n",
    "print(\"Remaining NaNs:\", df_logistic.isnull().sum().sum())\n",
    "print(\"TARGET missing:\", df_logistic[\"TARGET\"].isna().sum())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 34,
   "id": "3914a4c5-5be6-4d4f-9973-79577f36e6df",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "'\\nFor each fold (e.g. fold 1 of 5):\\n\\n    train split = folds 2,3,4,5  → fit models here\\n    val split   = fold 1         → predict here (these become OOF predictions)\\n\\n    For Logistic Regression specifically:\\n        1. fit imputer on train split → transform train split\\n        2. use same imputer          → transform val split\\n        3. fit scaler on train split → transform train split  \\n        4. use same scaler           → transform val split\\n        5. fit LR on transformed train split\\n        6. predict on transformed val split\\n'"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 34,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# >>> NOTE: median imputation + StandardScaler for the logistic branch are\n",
    "# intentionally NOT done here. They MUST be fit on the training split of each\n",
    "# CV fold and only applied to the validation split, otherwise statistics leak\n",
    "# from validation into training. The docstring below records that contract.\n",
    "\n",
    "# NOTE ON MEDIAN IMPUTATION: Before running the logistic cell we need the median imputation + StandardScaler step,\n",
    "# This was deliberately deferred. This must be done inside each CV fold to avoid leakage. \n",
    "\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "For each fold (e.g. fold 1 of 5):\n",
    "\n",
    "    train split = folds 2,3,4,5  → fit models here\n",
    "    val split   = fold 1         → predict here (these become OOF predictions)\n",
    "\n",
    "    For Logistic Regression specifically:\n",
    "        1. fit imputer on train split → transform train split\n",
    "        2. use same imputer          → transform val split\n",
    "        3. fit scaler on train split → transform train split  \n",
    "        4. use same scaler           → transform val split\n",
    "        5. fit LR on transformed train split\n",
    "        6. predict on transformed val split\n",
    "\"\"\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 35,
   "id": "98c9e154-6ffd-4408-b4fd-79c2fe5af470",
   "metadata": {},
