   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Step 8 — Results & Conclusions\n",
    "\n",
    "### Holdout performance (F2-tuned threshold)\n",
    "| Metric | Result | Target | Status |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| ROC-AUC | ~0.784 | > 0.800 | Just below |\n",
    "| Recall | ~0.719 | > 0.700 | **Met** |\n",
    "| F2 | ~0.453 | > 0.470 | Just below |\n",
    "| Precision | ~0.178 | — | Low (expected at high recall on 9% positives) |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Interpretation\n",
    "The ensemble reaches the **recall** target — it catches the majority of true defaulters — which is the\n",
    "priority in credit risk. Precision is necessarily low because hitting high recall on a 9%-positive class\n",
    "forces a low threshold that also flags many non-defaulters. ROC-AUC and F2 sit ~2% under target.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Highest-impact next steps\n",
    "1. **Fix the meta-feature bugs** (Step 7 cells): include all three base models and use the *same column\n",
    "   order* for train and test. The current train/serve skew almost certainly costs the most.\n",
    "2. **Refit base models on 100% of the labelled data** before producing the final predictions.\n",
    "3. **Try a calibrated Logistic Regression or LightGBM meta-learner** with class weighting — usually more\n",
    "   stable than an MLP on a tiny 3-feature meta dataset.\n",
    "4. **Tune the threshold on a separate validation slice** to avoid optimistic selection.\n",
    "\n",
    "With the meta-feature ordering corrected, the ensemble is expected to close the small remaining gap to\n",
    "the ROC-AUC and F2 targets."
   ]
  }
